[TEXT] **Root cause confirmed.** The startup log shows `eth0.10` was correctly brought UP during initialization (`ip link set eth0.10 up`), but it is currently **DOWN** — it has been taken down after startup (fault injection). There are zero RX bytes on `eth0.10`, confirming it is silently dropping all incoming VLAN 10 traffic from switch1. Meanwhile `eth0.20` is actively passing traffic (RX: 260 B / 4 pkts).

No repeated carrier transitions, no flap script — this is a clean **`link_down`** on `mswitch1.eth0.10`.

The chain is:
- pc4/pc5 → switch1 `br_vlan10` → `eth0.10` trunk to mswitch1 → **DEAD** — mswitch1 `eth0.10` **DOWN**
- laptop0 → switch1 `br_vlan20` → `eth0.20` trunk to mswitch1 → **ALIVE** — mswitch1 `eth0.20` UP ✓

